  <title>7.17.5: Equations of Graph Translations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02053</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.17.5: Equations of Graph Translations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>fb2cacf1-6fdd-44fa-b5df-3b583ff494f3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Here is a graph that represents \(y=x^2\). </para>
    <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/95133170df377117169b0f4e25c3315ccced783f"/></media></figure></para>
    <para>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. On the same coordinate plane, sketch a graph that represents \(y=(x−6)^2+10\). </para>
  <para>Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your Answer:</para>
  <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/65c1dd64b7648e12977967f98a128f35306943a2"/></media></figure></para>
  <para>A graph the same shape as \(y=x^2\) but shifted 6 units to the right and 10 units upward. Its vertex is at \((6,10)\).</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="2b8f3557-64d3-4c41-936f-4e80dfe421d9" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="fb53cb18-831e-4ec9-99db-988b82b6b351" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(y=-(x+2)^2−10\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=-(x+2)^2−10\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=(x+2)^2−10\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=-(x+2)^2+10\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=(x+2)^2+10\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The graph representing \(y=x^2\) is shifted 2 units to the left, 10 units down, and flipped so that it opens downward, as shown. </para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f92b9aa8f9d9d15e3e8bc3fda5ab1cec79e365b1"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Which equation defines this curve?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=-(x+2)^2−10\)</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
